  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Mongolia: Strengthening the Response to Gender-Based Violence - Phase II</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">1) To deepen technical knowledge of the specialized needs of marginalized groups, including women and girls in herder communities, through participatory research. 2) To enhance operationalization ofdomestic violence systems and services through the development of applied research. 3) To enhance the capacity of judges, prosecutors, advocates, police, and primary advice and legal aid assistance providers to apply a victim-centred approach. 4) To strengthen cooperation mechanisms in place across the justice chain that support a multidisciplinary approach. 5) To strengthen collective advocacy efforts with the Government of Mongolia to drive improvements in domestic violence-related legislation and services. 6) To raise awareness of legal rights, domestic violence services, and the importance of healthy, equitable relationships, especially among women, girls, and adolescent boys from nomadic herder communities. 7) To improve availability and accessibility of quality primary advice and legal assistance for victims / survivors of domestic violence from nomadic herder communities.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Direct beneficiaries: Community-based organizations, civil society organizations, local non-government organizations, primary advice and legal assistance providers, including Children, Family Development and Protection Agency specialists and inspectors, National Legal Institute paralegals and Mongolian Bar Association lawyers; judges; prosecutors, police representatives; women and girls. Indirect beneficiaries: Population of Mongolia.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project aims to enhance the capacity of Mongolian partners to mainstream a victim-centred approach and implement systems of cooperation to combat gender-based violence.</narrative>
  </description>
